      "writtenOn": "2026-03-05T02:35:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The for loop above already sanitizes duplicate spaces:\u2028\u2028\nExample inputs:\u2028\u2028“Hello   “ (with 3 spaces)\u2028\n\nThe for loop runs, for the character after o, bPrevSpace is false but becomes true as this character is a space, for the next space, bPrevSpace is true hence it is removed, finally for the third space bPrevSpace is true hence it is also removed.\u2028\u2028\n\nThis gives “Hello “ after the for loop\u2028\nAnd then just “Hello” after the if statement.\n\nI do not think this matters as well as this matches implimentations such as acrobat which also removes trailing spaces.",
      "parentUuid": "8fab50e5_bb5347d3",
      "revId": "e60065d41cf2589ef9c0b88b38e0690bb0627141",
      "serverId": "fca2d64a-0420-3532-b200-12848c95a47b"
